pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive direction of `reification_right_implication_negative_degree`: the
% big-M coefficient is `max(degree, 0)`, so a reification of a trivially true
% constraint is stored as trivially true, and the ordinary positive-degree
% encoding is unchanged. Constraint 4 pins the working case; constraint 3 pins
% a premise literal that shares a variable with the reified constraint;
% constraint 5 pins that a degree of i64::MIN is not pushed into a wider tier
% by a guard measuring a quantity the parser no longer computes.
f 5 ;
e x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 >= -1 : 1 ;
e x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 <= 5 : 2 ;
e x2 x3 ==> 1 x2 >= -1 : 3 ;
e x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 >= 1 : 4 ;
e x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 >= -9223372036854775808 : 5 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
